1
00:00:11,090 --> 00:00:12,490
Glow.

2
00:00:14,990 --> 00:00:19,990
I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince

3
00:00:14,990 --> 00:00:19,990
so I Can Take My Time
Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season

4
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:24,750
Episode 24: In the Light

5
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:30,250
<i>Well, that's funny. You blocked it?</i>

6
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:32,890
<i>Does that mean I'm onto something here?</i>

7
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:37,800
<i>Which would mean I could 
force you into turning good,</i>

8
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,520
<i>but those anti-symbols of 
yours are still trouble.</i>

9
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:45,930
<i>He's worried enough that he'll likely hold 
onto the anti-divine sorcery symbol.</i>

10
00:00:45,930 --> 00:00:47,990
<i>And with how delicate divine sorcery is,</i>

11
00:00:47,990 --> 00:00:50,770
<i>I can't try and sneak it through 
by using it like an enchantment...</i>

12
00:00:51,010 --> 00:00:55,030
<i>He can only create three 
types of symbol at once.</i>

13
00:00:55,030 --> 00:00:57,780
We're here, Prince Lloyd!

14
00:00:57,780 --> 00:01:00,030
Man, you're still not done yet?!

15
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:03,180
I know you're probably trying 
to take him alive, but—

16
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:05,660
He is not worthy of such mercy!

17
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:09,670
You guys...!

18
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:12,650
What brought that on?!

19
00:01:12,310 --> 00:01:13,390
YOINK

20
00:01:14,030 --> 00:01:16,130
You seem awfully relaxed.

21
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:22,810
Have you noticed the 
distortion in the singing?

22
00:01:23,070 --> 00:01:25,890
While I was discussing my past with you,

23
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:29,390
my chimeras have been marching 
towards the source of this song.

24
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:32,940
Shouldn't you be concerned about—

25
00:01:32,090 --> 00:01:33,570
I know.

26
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:37,830
Did you honestly think I hadn't noticed?

27
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,480
Burble

28
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,480
Burble

29
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,480
Burble

30
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:45,960
Burble

31
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:50,840
Burble

32
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,340
Burble

33
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:57,800
You don't have to hold it in.

34
00:02:01,770 --> 00:02:04,090
You can howl or scream if you want.

35
00:02:04,510 --> 00:02:06,440
It won't get in the way.

36
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,960
Your voice is lovely.

37
00:02:10,570 --> 00:02:14,360
We'll change the tune to match you, Shiro!

38
00:02:40,050 --> 00:02:43,930
Does this really sound like 
distortion to you, Guitane?!

39
00:02:43,930 --> 00:02:47,140
Because if it does, 
you're the one who doesn't get it!

40
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:50,570
I've got just the thing. A type of 
casting I'd been thinking about.

41
00:02:54,770 --> 00:02:56,470
I'm just a seventh prince.

42
00:02:57,480 --> 00:02:59,430
<i>Of all the absurdity...!</i>

43
00:03:00,090 --> 00:03:02,610
You'll want to put them 
together right now, Guitane.

44
00:03:02,610 --> 00:03:04,140
<i>How can he believe that?</i>

45
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:07,840
Symbols for earth, water, and wind elements.

46
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:11,460
<i>If not a god,
then what else could he possibly be?!</i>

47
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,080
Triple Incantation...

48
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:34,010
<i>I can only create three types 
of symbols at once... and so—</i>

49
00:03:34,750 --> 00:03:39,780
<i>if I use them for earth, water, 
and wind like he says,</i>

50
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:41,810
<i>I won't be able to guard 
against purifying effects.</i>

51
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:45,280
Purification

52
00:03:42,340 --> 00:03:45,280
<i>Which is why I absolutely can't</i>

53
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:47,290
<i>use up all my symbols.</i>

54
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:51,550
<i>It would result in my ultimate defeat.</i>

55
00:03:52,790 --> 00:03:55,550
<i>If the alternative is being 
"turned good" and taken alive...</i>

56
00:03:55,550 --> 00:03:57,370
<i>I would rather choose dea—</i>

57
00:04:03,790 --> 00:04:05,780
Earth, Water, Wind.

58
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:07,470
Excalibur!

59
00:04:12,930 --> 00:04:14,650
Triple Incantation:

60
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:19,360
Glacia Krystacier!

61
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:34,710
Beautiful...!

62
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:45,600
MMMMM

63
00:04:37,270 --> 00:04:39,820
Well blocked, Guitane!

64
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:41,750
This is bad, Prince Lloyd!

65
00:04:41,750 --> 00:04:45,600
I mean, I get it, 
but you're going totally overboard!

66
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:49,230
Are you mad, Seventh Prince?!

67
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:55,850
This spell has the potential to destroy 
the world, and wipe out humanity!

68
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:57,990
*View from the surface

69
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:57,990
*View from the surface

70
00:04:57,980 --> 00:05:00,600
Did the rain just turn into a blizzard?!

71
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:03,890
Mom, look! The sky looks nasty!

72
00:05:03,890 --> 00:05:05,830
It's the wrath of God!

73
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:07,990
The only person who could do this, etc...

74
00:05:05,830 --> 00:05:07,980
The only person who could manage this...

75
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:11,380
Oh, come on! After all this time, 
you're calling me a prince?

76
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:13,000
I thought I was a god!

77
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,840
There are no gods like you!

78
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,320
God is—

79
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:22,260
<i>Do I still... hold these expectations...</i>

80
00:05:22,730 --> 00:05:24,400
<i>of God?</i>

81
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:36,260
Shiro!

82
00:05:37,130 --> 00:05:39,620
I'm sorry we were late!

83
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:43,320
What do you think you're doing?

84
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:45,970
I thought you were on Guitane's side.

85
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:48,140
I'm not sure why you're here, either.

86
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:51,750
Who exactly is Bishop Guitane fighting?

87
00:05:51,750 --> 00:05:54,400
It's gotta be god. Who else?

88
00:05:56,410 --> 00:06:00,120
The almighty having to step in 
to stop a friend's rampage...

89
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:02,880
The world could end, and I 
wouldn't have a leg to stand on.

90
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:06,780
I agree. It's so very... frustrating.

91
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:15,120
<i>I'm so glad you're okay</i>

92
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:23,670
<i>Let's all eat pancakes together</i>

93
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:18,680
These lyrics are bizarre!

94
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:21,240
She's just freestyling now!

95
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:23,680
True! But it's still invigorating!

96
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:28,250
<i>Is a pure heart enough to allow anything?!</i>

97
00:06:28,250 --> 00:06:31,200
<i>What would that mean?! Inconsistency?! 
Or divine truth?!</i>

98
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:35,140
<i>Then look upon me, God!</i>

99
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:37,710
<i>I have broken so many taboos, 
become a beast...</i>

100
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:40,020
<i>Exploited the doubts of others,</i>

101
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:41,850
<i>betrayed my friends,</i>

102
00:06:41,850 --> 00:06:45,440
<i>and embroiled an innocent like Anastasia!</i>

103
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:48,580
<i>Just like her savage of a father!</i>

104
00:06:50,770 --> 00:06:54,710
<i>Look how far I have come, 
propelled by the purity of my rage!</i>

105
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:58,610
<i>Well?! What do you say?!</i>

106
00:07:03,430 --> 00:07:06,430
<i>O God... why?</i>

107
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:09,490
<i>Why don't you appear to judge me?</i>

108
00:07:09,850 --> 00:07:13,600
<i>How long will you let this continue?! 
Enough is enough!</i>

109
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:22,250
Poke

110
00:07:16,350 --> 00:07:19,500
<i>Then what about him, then? 
Will you allow this?!</i>

111
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:22,250
Cool

112
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:23,740
<i>The world is on the verge of being 
destroyed at the hands of an "innocent"!</i>

113
00:07:23,740 --> 00:07:27,840
<i>Surely such innocence is only being 
unaware of one's own wickedness!</i>

114
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:29,300
<i>This isn't...</i>

115
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:32,880
<i>the sort of thing that can be allowed!</i>

116
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:35,270
<i>It isn't worth protecting!</i>

117
00:07:35,270 --> 00:07:39,640
<i>Not a piece of it... holds any value!</i>

118
00:07:45,410 --> 00:07:46,650
Dad!

119
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:51,020
Mom, Dad's back!

120
00:07:51,020 --> 00:07:54,320
Oh, you didn't get lost on your way today?

121
00:07:54,650 --> 00:07:57,500
Mom, can I sing with Dad?

122
00:07:57,500 --> 00:08:00,970
Okay, why don't we all sing together, then?

123
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:06,250
<i>Dear God...</i>

124
00:08:11,490 --> 00:08:14,270
<i>This isn't fair.</i>

125
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:19,810
I shouldn't... Your dad's an awful singer.

126
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:26,140
Does it hurt, where you are? Are you lonely?

127
00:08:27,490 --> 00:08:31,220
<i>These days where, in my pure 
desire to deny purity...</i>

128
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:35,970
<i>were time I spent rejecting my past, 
when I felt the purest happiness.</i>

129
00:08:37,290 --> 00:08:39,060
You're so weird, Dad.

130
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:42,070
It's okay if you're bad!

131
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:46,840
Looks like dad's tired!

132
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:47,560
Yeah!

133
00:08:48,450 --> 00:08:50,650
I'm gonna get him!

134
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,470
<i>This willingness to come right at me...</i>

135
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:05,090
<i>You really are humoring me 
to the very end, aren't you?</i>

136
00:09:06,210 --> 00:09:09,610
Seventh Prince!

137
00:09:10,170 --> 00:09:12,730
Luma Maxima!

138
00:09:17,270 --> 00:09:20,220
<i>Even being struck by my Luma Maxima...</i>

139
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:25,680
<i>has no effect on him.</i>

140
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:29,990
Luma Maxima!

141
00:09:56,790 --> 00:09:58,360
It's warm.

142
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:01,650
This snow is healing my wounds!

143
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:05,010
<i>The inversion of a divine calamity...</i>

144
00:10:05,010 --> 00:10:08,830
<i>Is it even possible?
Purification on this scale...</i>

145
00:10:14,490 --> 00:10:17,180
It's raining again.

146
00:10:17,650 --> 00:10:20,630
It follows me around, you see.

147
00:10:21,140 --> 00:10:23,770
Maybe it's the heavens crying.

148
00:10:23,770 --> 00:10:25,140
Unlikely.

149
00:10:25,140 --> 00:10:29,140
I tend to think of it as being spat on.

150
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:34,300
I doubt the heavens will smile 
upon me until my day of death.

151
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:41,150
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

152
00:10:41,630 --> 00:10:45,980
I looked away the entire time... 
blaming god...

153
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:48,020
Taking advantage of your kindness...

154
00:10:49,370 --> 00:10:54,300
If I hadn't been there... if I had 
been able to stop my father...

155
00:10:55,190 --> 00:10:59,170
Maybe the rain was falling 
on me, all along...

156
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:04,640
Damn it, this is what I 
hate about purification.

157
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:07,230
People just can't keep stuff 
to themselves when it hits...

158
00:11:08,810 --> 00:11:09,510
Haugh

159
00:11:11,190 --> 00:11:15,430
Sorry for not noticing, kid.

160
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:24,600
<i>It's over, isn't it, Lloyd?</i>

161
00:11:25,450 --> 00:11:37,330
Super Confession Time, Brought to you by Purification

162
00:11:25,450 --> 00:11:37,330
Super Confession Time, Brought to you by Purification

163
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:28,970
Mommy! I'm sorry I didn't eat all my dinner.

164
00:11:28,970 --> 00:11:31,660
I'm sorry I drew on the wall, too.

165
00:11:31,660 --> 00:11:34,640
I should apologize for 
breaking Daddy's vase, too.

166
00:11:35,810 --> 00:11:37,330
Well, I guess it's fine!

167
00:11:40,510 --> 00:11:42,600
I'm still unsure...

168
00:11:43,030 --> 00:11:45,800
Whether or not the 
purification affected you,

169
00:11:43,690 --> 00:11:46,150
There, there, there.

170
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:50,230
or if this is what you were 
really like, all along.

171
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:56,270
You could've forced the other archbishops 
to go along with your plan if you'd wanted.

172
00:11:56,970 --> 00:11:58,770
So, why didn't you?

173
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:02,480
This Great Advent Festival...

174
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:05,590
If God did not descend,

175
00:12:05,590 --> 00:12:11,150
I expected them to bare their 
fangs at me, in His place.

176
00:12:11,490 --> 00:12:16,250
The ultimate arbiters of justice 
that I personally selected.

177
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:21,490
Should I overcome them...
or if they had defeated me...

178
00:12:21,490 --> 00:12:24,010
That would have been the 
point of the battle.

179
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:27,010
It needed to be in earnest...

180
00:12:27,010 --> 00:12:29,750
For both sides to see their 
ideals through to the end.

181
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:31,010
And even then...

182
00:12:31,380 --> 00:12:34,040
there were those who did not deny me.

183
00:12:34,650 --> 00:12:37,640
He's so dang serious...

184
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:37,200
He's so dang serious...

185
00:12:34,990 --> 00:12:40,410
In the end... the ones who stopped me 
was neither God, nor the bishops,

186
00:12:40,410 --> 00:12:45,830
but a seventh prince and a simple nun.

187
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:51,900
I'm sure that the gods must 
have blessed her voice.

188
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:54,210
Guess what, Guitane?

189
00:12:55,170 --> 00:12:58,800
Wanna know why Escher became a nun?

190
00:12:59,690 --> 00:13:02,800
Because I like singing.

191
00:13:04,790 --> 00:13:08,530
I-I mean, I respect God and everything, too!

192
00:13:08,530 --> 00:13:13,050
But since singing is the 
only thing I'm good at...

193
00:13:13,050 --> 00:13:18,380
the church seemed like the best place 
to sing in front of a lot of people.

194
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:20,570
And that's why you joined the clergy?

195
00:13:20,570 --> 00:13:25,820
B-But this Great Advent Festival 
is different from the usual!

196
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:29,260
Because it's revenge! 
Against that mean pastor!

197
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:32,320
Your singing
is barfaroonie...

198
00:13:26,190 --> 00:13:28,840
Your singing is barfaroonie.

199
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:32,320
Barf barf spew... Spew spew hurl...

200
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:34,450
And if he's going to show up, 
then I can't run away!

201
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:42,080
Hilarious, right? 
It's not even vaguely religious.

202
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:45,930
Maybe instead of worrying about what's 
wrong and right all the time,

203
00:13:45,930 --> 00:13:49,690
for once, you could think 
about what would be more fun?

204
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:54,750
I've spent my entire life living that way!

205
00:13:54,750 --> 00:13:58,850
I doubt anyone else could 
get away with that.

206
00:14:00,660 --> 00:14:05,100
<i>I mean, it killed me already. 
Once, in my past life, living like that.</i>

207
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:10,310
Just something I found.

208
00:14:13,810 --> 00:14:17,690
In the end... what did he say to you?

209
00:14:20,180 --> 00:14:21,460
I don't remember.

210
00:14:23,540 --> 00:14:27,210
I'll be waiting at Lordost Island, Guitane.

211
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:40,100
<i>The news shook Saloum.</i>

212
00:14:40,910 --> 00:14:44,270
<i>The Pope, Guitane, was murdered as part</i>

213
00:14:44,270 --> 00:14:46,940
<i>of a large-scale terrorist attack 
by an unidentified group.</i>

214
00:14:47,820 --> 00:14:51,700
<i>His body was discovered in one of 
their subterranean laboratories.</i>

215
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:57,280
<i>A man disguised as the Pope
 infiltrated the Great Advent Festival,</i>

216
00:14:57,280 --> 00:14:59,330
<i>acting as the mastermind 
behind the incident.</i>

217
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:04,480
<i>Was the motive some kind of 
rebellion against the gods?</i>

218
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:08,230
<i>The mysterious perpetrator's 
whereabouts remain unaccounted for.</i>

219
00:15:09,630 --> 00:15:11,250
This is so irritating!

220
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:14,920
Their whereabouts are "unaccounted for"?!

221
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:17,680
It was Pope Guitane who did it all!

222
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:19,450
Give it a rest, Rozelis.

223
00:15:19,940 --> 00:15:22,990
There are bishops who don't know the truth.

224
00:15:23,570 --> 00:15:25,430
We just need to keep our traps shut.

225
00:15:25,750 --> 00:15:28,390
Especially with how this could 
affect the Church's reputation.

226
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:31,200
If people start to question 
divine teachings...

227
00:15:31,570 --> 00:15:33,830
it could destroy the peace 
this nation enjoys.

228
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:37,300
Well, we can't leave things as-is anyway!

229
00:15:37,300 --> 00:15:40,450
The church needs a new 
leader to guide its flock!

230
00:15:40,450 --> 00:15:44,730
That being the case, I humbly 
accept the position of pope!

231
00:15:44,730 --> 00:15:46,450
That ain't happening.

232
00:15:47,270 --> 00:15:49,710
There's someone better I have in mind.

233
00:15:50,030 --> 00:15:54,070
Someone with overwhelming public 
support and charisma to boot.

234
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:56,600
Excuse me?

235
00:15:56,860 --> 00:16:02,090
Please, undertake the trial to become pope!

236
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:05,240
Who are you asking?

237
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:06,970
You!

238
00:16:06,970 --> 00:16:08,600
Why?

239
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:12,270
Because we want you to be the pope!

240
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:14,980
Huhhhh?!

241
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:18,370
Huuuh?!

242
00:16:42,410 --> 00:16:46,440
<i>My little brother sometimes 
appears in my room.</i>

243
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:50,950
<i>The fact that I won't tell anyone 
is probably convenient, for him.</i>

244
00:16:53,670 --> 00:16:59,630
Sorry. I did knock, but you were 
having such a good time playing...

245
00:16:55,490 --> 00:16:57,820
I'm leaving...

246
00:16:59,630 --> 00:17:04,040
Lloyd. You called it, back at the church.

247
00:17:05,090 --> 00:17:10,330
There's likely to be a major attack 
at the Great Advent Festival.

248
00:17:10,530 --> 00:17:13,590
When that happens, I believe 
that the two of you

249
00:17:13,590 --> 00:17:16,830
continuing the recital will have 
a major effect on the outcome.

250
00:17:18,030 --> 00:17:23,840
I'd like you to start playing when you feel 
like the town has become too loud to bear.

251
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:26,230
I'll arrange the stage for you.

252
00:17:27,610 --> 00:17:29,080
Why?

253
00:17:31,130 --> 00:17:33,360
Why tell only me all this?

254
00:17:34,540 --> 00:17:35,720
Because...

255
00:17:36,730 --> 00:17:40,860
If I told anyone else, they'd put a 
stop to it, because of the danger.

256
00:17:41,270 --> 00:17:42,400
That's true.

257
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:44,160
<i>Heretics.</i>

258
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:47,010
What did you think?

259
00:17:47,370 --> 00:17:49,920
Did the performance live up to your hopes?

260
00:17:50,990 --> 00:17:55,630
We both know who we are. 
And that there are things we'd die for.

261
00:17:55,630 --> 00:17:59,070
Yes! It was the best recital ever!

262
00:17:59,070 --> 00:18:02,130
<i>Subjects of obsession that we 
pursue to the point of heresy.</i>

263
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:06,000
You worked hard too, huh, Shiro?

264
00:18:07,330 --> 00:18:10,410
You're a good boy! And a strong boy!

265
00:18:09,310 --> 00:18:11,170
You did well, too.

266
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:24,370
<i>Spell notation?!</i>

267
00:18:24,370 --> 00:18:25,920
<i>She took my incantations...</i>

268
00:18:26,250 --> 00:18:29,500
<i>Even if she's only using tones, 
she was able to mimic them by ear?!</i>

269
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:34,870
Did you... happen to hear me, 
up above the clouds...?

270
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:39,540
I mean, I was hiding the whole time!

271
00:18:39,540 --> 00:18:41,920
I don't recognize any of this weird stuff!

272
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:42,790
Lloyd.

273
00:18:43,430 --> 00:18:46,940
The Great Advent Festival 
was fun, wasn't it?

274
00:18:47,390 --> 00:18:49,920
<i>There's no need for any questions.</i>

275
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:53,250
<i>Just like he won't get in my way,</i>

276
00:18:54,190 --> 00:18:56,610
<i>I don't intend on getting in his.</i>

277
00:18:57,700 --> 00:18:59,780
<i>No one can stop either of us.</i>

278
00:18:59,780 --> 00:19:04,760
<i>And I love these moments where we, 
as heretics, can spend time together.</i>

279
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:12,950
Where's the women's bath?!

280
00:19:09,950 --> 00:19:12,950
BOM BOM BOM

281
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:16,750
Lordost Island's newest attraction is perfect

282
00:19:16,030 --> 00:19:19,830
Why?! Why?!

283
00:19:16,750 --> 00:19:19,830
for washing away both mental 
and physical exhaustion!

284
00:19:19,830 --> 00:19:25,210
And the only person allowed to bathe co-ed 
at Seven Wolf Springs is Prince Lloyd!

285
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:23,840
No peeking allowed!

286
00:19:28,130 --> 00:19:30,220
Becoming the pope...

287
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:32,980
The spiritual leader of the people...

288
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:34,860
I really don't think I can handle it.

289
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:37,990
It's definitely a major responsibility.

290
00:19:37,990 --> 00:19:41,020
But it's amazing! I mean, becoming pope?!

291
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:42,740
Sounds dumb to me!

292
00:19:42,740 --> 00:19:46,740
You won't have time to see the 
guy you like, if that happens.

293
00:19:47,100 --> 00:19:48,690
What did Babylon say, anyway?

294
00:19:48,690 --> 00:19:51,610
Just, "I see."

295
00:19:51,610 --> 00:19:55,880
Wait, why would you bring him up?!

296
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:59,630
<i>I'd be sad if I couldn't 
see Lloyd anymore, too.</i>

297
00:19:59,630 --> 00:20:02,450
Talk about bittersweet!

298
00:20:02,450 --> 00:20:05,140
Then you've got Sylpha and Ren who are 
both head over heels for Lloyd...

299
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:06,730
I-I-I never said that!

300
00:20:06,730 --> 00:20:10,850
And you took part in that contest 
for a date with him, too, Tao!

301
00:20:10,850 --> 00:20:13,890
I was just doing that to mess with you two!

302
00:20:13,890 --> 00:20:15,610
Sylpha.

303
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:17,800
Can I go now?

304
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:19,360
You can not.

305
00:20:20,150 --> 00:20:23,520
Wh-Wh-What is Lloyd doing in here?!

306
00:20:22,570 --> 00:20:25,160
This happened before, didn't it?

307
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:29,580
Lloyd! At this rate, 
they're gonna make me the pope!

308
00:20:29,580 --> 00:20:31,570
What should I do?!

309
00:20:30,950 --> 00:20:33,160
An expression like
he's looking at a bug

310
00:20:31,570 --> 00:20:32,630
I see.

311
00:20:33,370 --> 00:20:38,620
If you're going to be that cold about 
it, I'll nominate your for pope!

312
00:20:38,620 --> 00:20:40,670
H-How'd you get that idea?!

313
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:45,290
Prince Albert was bragging to Bishop Dante

314
00:20:45,290 --> 00:20:50,300
about how you helped resolve this 
incident with your brilliant deductions!

315
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:49,620
My little brother's an ace detective!

316
00:20:49,470 --> 00:20:50,950
He's the second
candidate for Pope.

317
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:53,430
<i>That stupid brother...!</i>

318
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:58,570
I'm afraid not! Prince Lloyd is going to 
live peacefully at the castle, with me!

319
00:20:58,570 --> 00:21:01,060
He is not going to be put 
on display for the world!

320
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:02,080
On display?!

321
00:21:02,080 --> 00:21:03,700
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

322
00:21:05,330 --> 00:21:08,030
It means being put on display...?

323
00:21:09,020 --> 00:21:11,340
That sounds right up your alley, Escher.

324
00:21:11,340 --> 00:21:12,690
Being on display.

325
00:21:12,690 --> 00:21:14,340
Saria?

326
00:21:14,950 --> 00:21:18,120
That's not me. It's a rock.

327
00:21:19,950 --> 00:21:21,370
Do you remember...

328
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:25,740
that time I played a 
recital at the church...?

329
00:21:25,740 --> 00:21:29,290
Please let me sing with you!

330
00:21:28,390 --> 00:21:29,290
No.

331
00:21:31,810 --> 00:21:34,010
Let me sing with you!

332
00:21:34,470 --> 00:21:39,310
How you chased after me for days, 
demanding we perform a duet?

333
00:21:39,310 --> 00:21:43,190
I just... really wanted 
to sing with your music.

334
00:21:44,010 --> 00:21:48,730
There are so many guests 
for your recitals, Saria.

335
00:21:48,730 --> 00:21:52,970
And if I was able to make those 
people happy with my singing...

336
00:21:53,700 --> 00:21:56,440
I'd just be so thrilled.

337
00:21:59,710 --> 00:22:03,630
Are you saying you intend to use the 
church and myself as a platform?

338
00:22:03,630 --> 00:22:05,850
Oh, no! Not at all!

339
00:22:08,790 --> 00:22:10,960
It won't just be a lot of people.

340
00:22:11,350 --> 00:22:13,720
Your singing would be heard...

341
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:15,680
around the world.

342
00:22:23,340 --> 00:22:25,930
If you use the platform of being the pope.

343
00:22:27,580 --> 00:22:29,110
Saria...

344
00:22:29,740 --> 00:22:33,270
That's not me. It's a duckie.

345
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:38,160
<i>That's true. She's exactly right.</i>

346
00:22:38,710 --> 00:22:40,880
<i>Everyone will be listening...</i>

347
00:22:46,050 --> 00:22:47,870
<i>to my song!</i>

